From f819689fa43a2fae0c94940ebf9cbd9d3c8aba06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 05:23:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] check(jini-guard): revert two optional-peer moves and the
 per-call SVG sanitizer

- oauth: openid-client/oauth4webapi back to dependencies. As optional peers, a fresh
  install of @jini-ai/agent-runtime fails (agent-runtime tests/loads-without-integrations:
  Cannot find package 'openid-client' from @jini-ai/oauth/dist/discovery.js), 11 tests red.
- diagnostics: js-tokens back to dependencies. ./observability (otel.ts -> core/secrets-only)
  needs it, and existing consumers import that entry without declaring js-tokens.
- cms sanitize-svg: the factory rewrite made every sanitizeSvg() call build and close its own
  JSDOM (measured 8.3 ms vs 1.1 ms per call); no caller used the factory, and hosts sanitize
  SVG per public media request. Restored the e5f49697 module-lazy runtime.
These reopen 3 SI-dependency + 1 HW3 guard findings, left for an owner decision.
pnpm-lock.yaml regenerated with pnpm install.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
